 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "수량 표현 a few / a little / a lot of / not many / not much",
   "en": "quantifiers: a few, a little, a lot of, not many, not much"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "셀 수 있는 명사(복수)에는 a few, many를, 셀 수 없는 명사에는 a little, much를 씁니다. a lot of는 둘 다 쓸 수 있습니다. 부정문이나 의문문에서는 many / much를 주로 씁니다 (I don't have many friends. How much money?).",
   "en": "Use a few and many with plural countable nouns, and a little and much with uncountable nouns. A lot of works with both. In negatives and questions use many / much (I don't have many friends. How much money?)."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "a few + 복수",
     "I have a few friends."
    ],
    [
     "a little + 불가산",
     "I drink a little milk."
    ],
    [
     "a lot of",
     "He has a lot of books."
    ],
    [
     "not many / not much",
     "I don't have many friends. I don't have much time."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "a few ≈ 몇 개 (있다), few만 쓰면 거의 없음.",
    "en": "a few = some; few alone = hardly any."
   },
   {
    "ko": "a little ≈ 조금 (있다), little만 쓰면 거의 없음.",
    "en": "a little = some; little alone = hardly any."
   },
   {
    "ko": "긍정문에서는 much / many 대신 a lot of를 많이 씁니다.",
    "en": "In positive sentences a lot of is more natural than much / many."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "I have a few friends.",
    "ko": "나는 친구가 몇 명 있어요."
   },
   {
    "t": "I drink a little milk.",
    "ko": "나는 우유를 조금 마셔요."
   },
